#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_rational

#% text
# `is_rational(x)` gives `true` when `x` is an exact rational number, an integer or a fraction, else `false`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_rational(2/3)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_rational(4)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_rational(0.5)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Exact irrational numbers are not rational:

#% cell
[is_rational(sqrt(2)), is_rational(pi)]
#% output
#= [false, false]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_integer`, `numerator`, `denominator`, `rationalize`
